---
description: Observability rules for metrics, logs, traces, and alerting
globs: [
  "observability/**",
  "ops/**",
  "telemetry/**",
  ".github/workflows/*observability*.yml",
  ".github/workflows/*telemetry*.yml",
  "**/logging/**",
  "**/metrics/**",
  "**/tracing/**",
  "infra/**"
]
alwaysApply: false
---

- Emit structured, leveled logs; avoid secrets/PII and include correlation/request IDs.
- Define SLOs for critical user journeys; derive SLIs from user-visible outcomes.
- Add metrics for throughput, latency (pXX), errors, and saturation; prefer RED/USE patterns for services.
- Use tracing for key flows; propagate context across services and queues.
- Alerts should be actionable, routed to owners, and tested; avoid noisy or unactionable signals.
- Include health/readiness checks and surface deploy/version metadata in telemetry.
- Keep dashboards lightweight and tied to SLOs; annotate with deploys/incidents.
